Z||000028||Ken Wittlief||08-28-2001||03:15 PM||||the longest phrase I could come up with that reads the same upside down is:<P>Pompous snodwod<P> I was thinking of naming my hobiecat that, cause when you capsize the boat, the name would still be readable upsidedown - ended up naming it HydroManiac instead<P>it takes very little voltage to kill yourself - a kid electocuted himself once with an ohm meter, which was powered by an ordinary 9 volt battery, when he put it on ohms and stuck the leads in his ears. The current flow through his brain stopped his heart and he died.<P>I think all the words in the phonetic alphabet dont ryme with anything: Alpha, Beta, Charlie, Delta, Echo, Foxtrot... thats why they use it, cause B sounds like D,E,G,P,T,V, and Z so on a bad radio channel you can not mistake BETA for anything...||||reg||10
